BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 381 2990 Tm (Mean radius is the average distance of every shot from the center of the group.) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 381 3113 Tm (Measure how far each shot is from the center, add those distances up, and divide by the number of shots. That is) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 381 3201 Tm (the mean radius. It uses every shot, not just two, so one lucky or unlucky shot moves it less.) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 381 3324 Tm (For five shots, mean radius and extreme spread are about equally jumpy. The difference shows as you shoot) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 381 3412 Tm (more: mean radius settles down and extreme spread keeps wandering, because extreme spread only ever looks) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 381 3500 Tm (at the two worst shots. That is why GroupLab leads with mean radius. There is more in the article Mean radius or) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 381 3588 Tm (extreme spread? \(https://grouplab.org/research/mean-radius-or-extreme-spread/\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 381 3711 Tm (At the range. For the same rifle, mean radius is a bit more than a third of the extreme spread of a five-shot group.) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 381 3799 Tm (Compare mean radius with mean radius, never with somebody's extreme spread.) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 381 3922 Tm (In GroupLab. Mean radius is in the six figures in view, with its range.) Tj ET
