BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 381 1808 Tm (A flyer is a shot far from the rest, and in a large group one shot well out is normal, not a mistake.) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 381 1931 Tm (The more shots you fire, the farther out the worst one will usually be. In a five-shot group from a perfectly steady) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 381 2019 Tm (rifle, the worst shot is typically about one and two thirds mean radii from the center. In a twenty-shot group it is) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 381 2107 Tm (about two mean radii, and in thirty a little more. So a shot that sits out on its own is often just the rifle being a rifle.) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 381 2230 Tm (Calling a shot a flyer and leaving it out makes the group look better than the rifle is. Leave a shot out only when) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 381 2318 Tm (you know why it went wide: you flinched, the rest moved, or the wind gusted.) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 381 2441 Tm (At the range. Note why a shot went wide while you remember. Without a reason, keep it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 381 2564 Tm (In GroupLab. Click a hole to call it a flyer, with your reason; the Worst shot card says whether it is farther out than) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 381 2652 Tm (chance would put it.) Tj ET
